          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "For mid-market organisations (typically 50 to 500+ employees), selecting an AI consultant requires finding a partner that avoids both **lightweight SMB chatbot builders** (who often lack enterprise data governance) and **Tier-1 global consultancies** (whose overhead and delivery timelines can be excessive). \n\nConsultancies operating in Melbourne with strong practices around **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **AI agent architectures**, and **practical workflow automation (Power Platform / M365)** include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Eagle360 Consulting\n* **Melbourne Location:** Collins St / CBD presence (Melbourne & Sydney).\n* **Core Focus:** Explicitly caters to the Australian **mid-market segment**. They focus on building governed Copilot Studio agents, Power Automate flows, and low-code apps tied directly into business systems like Dynamics 365 Business Central, CRM, and SQL.\n* **Best For:** Mid-market firms wanting structured, fixed-price practical deployments (e.g., connecting AI agents to core ERP/finance and operations workflows).\n\n### 2. IOTAI\n* **Melbourne Location:** Level 6, 607 Bourke Street, Melbourne.\n* **Core Focus:** A modern AI and workflow automation consultancy with dedicated offerings segmented specifically for mid-market companies (50–200 seats). They specialize in Microsoft Copilot Studio agents, hybrid workflow automation (integrating Copilot Studio with orchestration tools like n8n or Power Automate), and internal process transformation.\n* **Best For:** Practical, rapid-ROI agent deployments across HR, operations, customer support, and administrative workflow automation.\n\n### 3. Professional Advantage\n* **Melbourne Location:** Level 5, 469 La Trobe Street, Melbourne.\n* **Core Focus:** One of Australia’s longest-standing mid-market Microsoft Solutions Partners. They have an established **Copilot Studio Consulting Practice** dedicated to planning, building, and governing autonomous and conversational agents inside Microsoft 365.\n* **Best For:** Established mid-tier firms that require strong data security, Microsoft 365 compliance, and integration with Power Apps/SharePoint ecosystems.\n\n### 4. Antares Solutions\n* **Melbourne Location:** Melbourne / East Coast team.\n* **Core Focus:** Well-regarded for Microsoft Modern Workplace and Power Platform engineering. They specialize in turning everyday operational bottlenecks (forms, multi-step approvals, reporting) into automated workflows backed by Copilot Studio and Power Automate.\n* **Best For:** Organisations seeking strict Centre of Excellence (CoE) governance to prevent \"Power Platform sprawl\" while deploying autonomous internal agents.\n\n### 5. C9 \n* **Melbourne Location:** Melbourne CBD & National.\n* **Core Focus:** Pure-play Microsoft automation and software development firm focusing on Copilot Studio custom agents. They specialize in building custom API connectors, adaptive cards, and context-aware agents that query internal knowledge bases and ERPs securely.\n* **Best For:** Custom integrations where standard off-the-shelf Copilot prompts need to trigger real-time actions across multiple line-of-business APIs.\n\n---\n\n### What to Verify Before Engaging a Partner\n\nWhen vetting a Melbourne consultant for a mid-market Copilot Studio rollout, confirm:\n1. **M365 & SharePoint Permissions Audit:** Copilot Studio agents inherit your internal access controls. A capable partner will start with a data hygiene and permission review to ensure agents do not surface confidential HR or executive data to unauthorized staff.\n2. **Action-Oriented Architecture (Agentic AI):** Ensure they build agents that **take actions** via Power Automate cloud flows or custom API connectors, rather than just basic Q&A retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chatbots.\n3. **Licensing Transparency:** Mid-market rollouts often involve understanding the cost distinction between *Microsoft 365 Copilot add-ons*, *Copilot Studio message capacity packs*, and *Power Apps/Dataverse premium licensing*. Experienced consultants will model these costs upfront.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
